            <ArticleTitle>Left-ventricular aneurysm in a young male due to spontaneous coronary artery dissection.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>364-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of spontaneous coronary artery dissection in a 26-year-old male with subsequent left-ventricular aneurysm is reported. A coronary bypass operation using left internal mammary artery combined with left-ventricular aneurysmectomy was performed successfully. This is the youngest case in the literature which describes a successful surgical treatment for a spontaneous coronary artery dissection with left-ventricular aneurysm.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
